# Step 18: the repository map, in cortex-index, and what it added to
# cortex-agent (the map in an epoch), cortex-tools (the outline tool) and
# cortex-core (the index of a session).
#
# Each rule is broken here: the extractors' nesting, the cache's
# invalidation, the caps, the walk's ignore rules, links and gate, the
# map's budget and its stability, the map's place in an epoch and in what
# a summary replays, the start-up path, and the outline tool's workspace.

[break] a-brace-language-drops-nested-definitions
rule: A definition whose body holds others (a type, an impl, an interface, a module) has what is inside it outlined, one level deeper.
file: crates/cortex-index/src/extract/brace.rs
find: Body::Holds => Frame::Holds { entry: done.entry },
replace: Body::Holds => Frame::Opaque { entry: done.entry },
caught-by:
    cortex-index extract::tests::methods_nest_in_their_impl_and_class_in_every_brace_language
    cortex-index::it outlines::rust

[break] an-indentation-language-drops-nested-definitions
rule: In Python and Ruby a class or a module holds what is indented under it; only a function's body is opaque.
file: crates/cortex-index/src/extract/indent.rs
in: Blocks::opaque
find: self.open.iter().any(|open| open.opaque)
replace: !self.open.is_empty()
caught-by:
    cortex-index extract::tests::methods_nest_in_their_class_in_the_indentation_languages
    cortex-index::it outlines::python
    cortex-index::it outlines::ruby

[break] a-function-body-is-outlined
rule: Nothing inside a function's body is outlined: a local struct or a closure is not a definition of the file.
